WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.190
Until Disney decides to release another trilogy
in the mainline series, Star Wars Episode

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:10.150
IX: The Rise of Skywalker is the final bow
on the 42-year package that is the Skywalker

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.150
Saga.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.570
And while it answers a lot of longstanding
questions, it also raises just as many questions

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.660
as it answers.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.080
Here are some of the big ones, and — of
course — spoilers are ahead.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.960
One burning question the movie answers within
its opening minutes is whether Emperor Palpatine

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:25.970
is alive.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.189
And he is!

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:30.259
He's not a force ghost and not identified
as a clone.

00:00:30.259 --> 00:00:35.700
He's the full-on flesh-and-blood Sheev Palpatine,
being kept alive by a very tall, mechanical

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.220
life support system.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:42.140
Nothing he communicates to Kylo Ren, Rey or
General Pryde mention any words about how

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.580
he survived being thrown down a giant pit
at the end of Return of the Jedi.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.180
Nobody bothers to ask him, either.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.871
Everybody who now knows the emperor is back
including Luke Skywalker's force ghost, who

00:00:52.871 --> 00:00:57.170
you'd think would really be curious to learn
how Palpatine made it out of that pickle just

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.390
kind of rolls with it.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:03.800
Even the Resistance spends only a few minutes
being incredulous before simply accepting

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.080
Palpatine is alive and kicking.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.520
"No.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.540
No.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:08.540
No.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.440
You will die!"

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.030
Rise of Skywalker's biggest revelation is
the truth of Rey's parentage.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.750
After meeting Palpatine on the Sith planet
Exegol, Kylo Ren learns that what he knew

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.490
about Rey's parents was only partially true:
Yes, they sold her.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.720
Yes, they were basically nobody.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.130
But it was all intentional.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:34.390
They made themselves anonymous and left Rey
behind because her father was Emperor Palpatine's

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:37.530
son, making Rey the Emperor's granddaughter.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.520
But hold up a minute: Emperor Palpatine had
a son?

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:41.520
When?

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.170
Let's try to work it out: If the Emperor's
family ages like other humans, Rey is probably

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:50.890
in her early 20s by the time Rise of Skywalker
takes place, which would mean her father would

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:56.150
probably have been born 40 to 50 years earlier,
given how he looks in the flashbacks.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:00.700
So Palpatine Jr. would have probably been
born sometime between the prequel trilogy

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.370
and the original trilogy.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.130
So where was he during the original trilogy?

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.590
Who was his mother?

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:11.319
Was the younger Palpatine a clone, like his
illegitimate son in the old Extended Universe?

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:15.000
It isn't addressed, so your guesses are as
good as anyone else's.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.160
"Long have I waited."

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.780
That ominous statement from Emperor Palpatine
is essentially his greeting to his granddaughter,

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.780
Rey.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.880
But why spend decades just sitting around
on Exegol?

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:31.130
Presumably he was waiting for his fleet of
planet-exploding Star Destroyers to be finished,

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:35.080
but we're also told he tried to have Rey brought
to him when she was just a child.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.069
So what really was his plan?

00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:39.520
Why did he need to create Snoke to be his
puppet?

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.300
Could he not have shown back up and started
the First Order himself?

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.849
Perhaps he was too physically weak, but he
was hearty enough to create all those Snoke

00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:48.849
clones.

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:52.840
Why did he have to use Kylo Ren as his intermediary
rather than going directly to Rey?

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.040
She may have been well-hidden for a while,
but eventually she made herself very well

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.040
known.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.370
Why did Palpatine's plan have to be so complicated?

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:03.280
"Sometimes I just don't understand human behavior."

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.790
Rey and the gang find a dagger on Ochi's ship
that has the directions to one of the Sith

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.480
wayfinders written on it.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:15.360
But there's a catch: it's written in the ancient
Sith language, and that's not something they

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.770
teach in scavenger school on Jakku.

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:23.040
C-3PO is able to read it, but can't relay
a translation to his pals because his programming

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.040
forbids it.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.910
When he starts to explain that there are some
legalities behind that prohibition involving

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:31.629
the Galactic Senate, Poe cuts him off before
he can get into the details.

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:37.600
Our heroes get around that roadblock by having
droidsmith Babu Frik do a potentially dangerous

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:42.150
and definitely unethical procedure to extract
the information.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.640
But let's back up a bit: How does C-3PO know
Sith?

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:50.900
By the time Anakin Skywalker built the droid
from spare parts, Sithspeak would seemingly

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:55.660
have only been a language used by the highly
secretive Sith Order, which had been in hiding

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.129
for hundreds of years.

00:03:57.129 --> 00:04:02.600
Maybe C-3PO's parts were really, really old,
and from a time when Sith was a lot more common.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.080
Or maybe his language software is just really,
really good.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.520
Sheev Palpatine knows how to play to a crowd.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:12.100
He drew thunderous applause while liberty
died, remember?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:17.239
He similarly gets his audience of black-robed
figures white hot with excitement as he dares

00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:19.889
Rey to strike him down on Exegol.

00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:23.650
He has them eating right out of his horribly
disfigured hands.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.009
Just one question, though: Who are the people
in the stands?

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:31.729
They're almost assuredly Sith of one type
or another, since Exegol is the secret Sith

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:34.150
homeworld, but are they living creatures?

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:36.550
Are they more beings he created, like he did
Snoke?

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:40.490
Are they the spirits of all the Sith who lived
in the past?

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:43.460
Palpatine says he contains all of the Sith
within him.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:44.460
Is that them?

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.640
Did they build his fleet of planet-exploding
star destroyers?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.600
Where did they go?

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:53.160
Rey claims the name Skywalker at the end of
the movie, making her at least one of the

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.900
Skywalkers who rise in the movie.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:59.970
She uses the combined force energy of every
Jedi who ever put on a robe to defeat her

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.280
grandfather, deflecting his own force lightning
back at him.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.039
And she helps redeem Ben Solo.

00:05:05.039 --> 00:05:06.810
She does a lot of good things.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:12.029
But Palpatine makes the deal very clear: If
she kills him, she becomes the empress.

00:05:12.029 --> 00:05:17.419
So even though she doesn't absorb his life
force like he planned, isn't she the empress?

00:05:17.419 --> 00:05:18.499
By birthright?

00:05:18.499 --> 00:05:19.979
By the order of succession?

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:22.059
There's no Republic to go back to any longer.

00:05:22.059 --> 00:05:23.159
They got wiped out.

00:05:23.159 --> 00:05:28.280
Sure, Rey may just dissolve everything and
start a new New Republic, but there's a slew

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.719
of First Order and Final Order loyalists out
there desperate for a leader to tell them

00:05:32.719 --> 00:05:33.719
what to do.

00:05:33.719 --> 00:05:38.279
It may be Rey's responsibility to say, if
nothing else, "Hit the bricks."

00:05:38.279 --> 00:05:39.559
"OK."

00:05:39.559 --> 00:05:42.569
Heavy is the head that wears the hood, right?

